    perf(arty): skip redundant same-worker wake (#931)
    
    ## Summary
    
    - Add `TaskSet::is_executing` to expose the executor's existing cycle
    state.
    - Skip the worker wake when direct same-worker registration occurs
    during that cycle.
    - Keep the wake for timer, driver, and other callbacks that register
    work outside the executor cycle.
    - Add integration coverage for the public executor state and private
    worker coverage for both wake paths.
    
    ## Motivation
    
    Direct same-worker registration adds the child to the executor task set.
    The executor observes this new work before it decides whether to
    continue or suspend. Waking the same worker during that cycle leaves an
    unnecessary notification for later processing.
    
    Arty now reads the cycle state from `TaskSet::is_executing`. This avoids
    a second cycle marker in Arty and keeps the state with the executor that
    owns it.
    
    ## Performance evidence
    
    Two longer Criterion pairs used a 5-second warm-up, a 10-second
    measurement window, and 100 samples per case.
    
    The one-worker nested retained-waker workload improved by 2.64% and
    4.72%. The average improvement was 3.69%. The 95% confidence intervals
    did not overlap in either pair.
    
    The host was not isolated because another session was active. Other
    one-worker and multi-worker results were inconsistent. Treat this
    evidence as directional, not as a general wall-clock performance claim.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - `cargo test -p arty_executor --test lifecycle
    task_set_execution_state_follows_the_owner_cycle`
    - `cargo test -p arty --lib
    same_worker_child_progresses_without_a_redundant_worker_notification`
    - `cargo test -p arty --lib
    timer_callback_direct_submission_notifies_worker`
    - `cargo check -p arty_executor -p arty`
    
    The pull request checks provide the exhaustive validation.
    
    ## Risk
    
    The wake change affects only direct registration on the current Arty
    worker during an active executor cycle. Registration outside that cycle
    still wakes the worker.
    
    `TaskSet::is_executing` is for a live executor task set on its owner
    thread. This change does not add executor identity tracking or special
    thread-local teardown handling. Shutdown, task placement, and result
    delivery are unchanged.
    
