    refactor(arty): unify task completion and shutdown (#899)
    
    ## Summary
    
    Adopting the runtime panic policy exposed defects in task completion and
    shutdown coordination. This change fixes those defects with a simpler
    internal design.
    
    - Replace executor-driven completion polling with a push-based
    completion model. Tasks send completion directly to their handles.
    - Route panic, explicit, and worker shutdown through one coordinated
    runtime shutdown path.
    - Wake async workers when blocking work triggers panic shutdown.
    - Preserve panic results, shutdown causes, and telemetry across races
    between completion and shutdown.
    - Remove duplicated task and join APIs from `arty_executor`.
    - Make registered work more flexible to consume. The caller chooses
    whether it needs a local or remote handle.
    - Simplify task preparation and handle ownership.
    
    ## Impact
    
    The push-based model removes executor-side completion polling and
    reduces work in the execution cycle. This improves performance and makes
    shutdown behavior easier to reason about.
    
    The public API of `arty` does not change. The lower-level
    `arty_executor` API changes to remove duplicated APIs and support the
    new completion model. The change adds coverage for panic policy,
    concurrent panics, shutdown races, worker wake-up, and task completion
    behavior.
    
    ## Validation
    
