    feat(arty_executor)!: propagate shutdown causes (#880)
    
    ## Motivation
    
    A runtime shutdown has one authoritative cause. Modeling that cause once
    makes the shutdown flow easier to follow because every worker, task,
    join, and runtime error refers to the same reason instead of
    reconstructing or losing it at each boundary.
    
    This model also prepares Arty for its planned panic policy. When the
    runtime is configured to shut down on the first unhandled panic, that
    panic can become the single shutdown cause and propagate through the
    existing cancellation and error paths.
    
    ## Summary
    
    - add cloneable `arty_executor::ShutdownCause` and `ShutdownError`
    values that preserve the original typed error and source chain
    - change `arty_executor::Executor::begin_shutdown` and
    `TaskSet::begin_shutdown` to accept the authoritative shutdown cause
    - make `arty_executor::JoinError` a public `Panicked` / `Shutdown` enum
    and propagate caused cancellation through it
    - add a crate-internal cloneable Arty `Shutdown` state that publishes
    the first cause once
    - model Arty join handles internally as pending, immediate-error, or
    completed without changing their public API
    - propagate runtime, worker, and I/O failures into executor and Arty
    `JoinError` source chains
    - include caused runtime failures in `#[arty::main]` and `#[arty::test]`
    panic messages when shutdown cancels the root task
    
    ## Shutdown semantics
    
    The first shutdown request is authoritative. A cause-free request
    remains cause-free even if a later request supplies an error. Later
    shutdown requests are idempotent and cannot overwrite the first cause.
    
    `ShutdownError` keeps the original error as a shared immutable source
    rather than converting it to text. Local and remote task cancellation,
    rejected submissions, retained task sets, executor drop, runtime stop,
    worker failures, and I/O failures use the same cause.
    
    Arty stores the cause in a shared `OnceLock<ShutdownCause>`. The cell is
    both the shutdown-state indicator and the cause publication mechanism.
    
    ## Audit
    
    The shutdown audit covered explicit stop, runtime and executor drop,
    worker panic, contained task panic, startup and I/O initialization
    failure, I/O cycle failure, final timer panic, driver shutdown, blocking
    work, queued and running tasks, local and remote rejection, retained
    schedulers/task sets/joins/wakers, repeated and concurrent requests, and
    exact-once task and driver teardown.
    
    The rebase preserves the merged scheduler improvements from #855:
    intrusive task ownership, `ExecutorShared`, per-worker remote result
    pools, and pooled remote factories. Shutdown causes are integrated into
    those owners without restoring the removed `ExecutorCore` design.
    
    ## Breaking changes
    
    `arty_executor::Executor::begin_shutdown` and `TaskSet::begin_shutdown`
    now require a `ShutdownCause`. `arty_executor::JoinError` is now a
    public enum, replacing its classification and extraction methods with
    direct variant matching. Breaking changes are allowed in
    `arty_executor`. The public `arty` API has no breaking change.
    
    ## Tests and validation
    
    - `cargo check -p arty_executor -p arty`
    - `cargo test -p arty_executor --test join_lifecycle`
    - focused Arty unit tests for runtime workers, dispatch, task
    preparation, and join failure states
    - public Arty integration tests for scheduler, I/O failure, worker
    panic, and shutdown cause propagation
    - `just anvil-fmt --fix`
    - `just anvil-readme --fix`
    - `just anvil-spellcheck`
    
    The comprehensive pre-rebase validation also covered full
    affected-package tests and doctests, Clippy with `-D warnings`, public
    API and external-type checks, package verification, and Miri. The pull
    request pipeline runs the complete post-rebase matrix after each update.
    
    ## Adversarial reviews
    
    Two independent implementation reviews found and drove fixes for cause
    publication visibility, authoritative error precedence, API
    compatibility, unwind auto-traits, error wrapper surface, and test
