    perf(observed): reduce enrichment allocations and instructions (#877)
    
    ## Why
    
    Enrichment context is installed on every poll of attached and enriched
    futures, and composite sinks traverse their leaves for every emitted
    event. Repeated temporary allocations, reference-count operations, and
    iterator bookkeeping add cost directly to these hot paths.
    
    ## What changed
    
    - Retain transfer restoration scratch storage across attached-future
    polls, including transfers that spill beyond the inline slot capacity.
    - Cache one enrichment-chain node per sink slot in an enriched future
    and reuse it while it remains exclusively owned.
    - Evict a cached node when a transfer captures it, so captured context
    remains an immutable snapshot and later polls rebuild independent state.
    - Clear dynamic parent links after each poll to avoid retaining
    unrelated enrichment chains.
    - Traverse the flattened composite sink slice directly during sampling
    and dispatch while preserving processor bit ordering and the two-phase
    event construction boundary.
    - Preserve the early return for dedicated and processor-free sinks so
    disabled telemetry does not read dynamic event metadata.
    - Expand metabench coverage for one, three, and eight sink slots across
    attached polling, warmed enriched polling, captured enrichment polling,
    context capture, and composite event traversal.
    
    ## Compatibility
    
    This preserves the public API and existing context-propagation contract.
    Transfer guard lifetimes, structured event fields, redaction and
    sensitivity handling, processor routing, sampling, disabled-sink
    behavior, and telemetry semantics are unchanged.
    
    ## Performance evidence
    
    The comparison used the same final benchmark harness on the PR base
    (`9a57c0b0`) and head. It ran under WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04 with Valgrind
    3.22.0 and Rust 1.96.1. Gungraun instruction counts and metabench
    allocation probes are deterministic; no wall-clock timing claims are
    made from this shared environment.
    
    ### Gungraun instructions
    
    | Workload | Base | Head | Change |
    |---|---:|---:|---:|
    | Attached poll, 1 slot | 197 | 158 | 19.8% fewer |
    | Attached poll, 3 slots | 399 | 378 | 5.3% fewer |
    | Attached poll, 8 slots | 1,150 | 965 | 16.1% fewer |
    | Warm enriched future, 8 polls, 1 sink | 3,193 | 1,593 | 50.1% fewer |
    | Warm enriched future, 8 polls, 3 sinks | 12,697 | 3,769 | 70.3% fewer
    |
    | Warm enriched future, 8 polls, 8 sinks | 39,046 | 9,689 | 75.2% fewer
    |
    | Event traversal, 1 sink | 280 | 270 | 3.6% fewer |
    | Event traversal, 3 sinks | 689 | 682 | 1.0% fewer |
    | Event traversal, 8 sinks | 1,659 | 1,672 | 0.8% more |
    
