    allocation on both measured x64 hosts. This is requested heap storage,
    not RSS or allocator size classes, and not a stable layout promise. The
    high-core cancellation workload motivates the fixed sharding cost.
    Cancellation releases wakers/task references while retaining reusable
    storage.
    
    Channel/watch value borrows remain exclusive so Send-but-not-Sync
