    ## Design
    
    - exposes runtime-bound I/O context access through `Builtins::io()`
    - keeps worker affinity and external-thread dispatch in Arty while
    delegating registry and driver mechanics to `arty_io_host`
    - initializes each worker-local driver lazily when that worker first
    retrieves the registered context
    - uses runtime-assigned roles: the first registered context type is
    primary and later types are secondary
    - runs secondary drivers before the primary and gives secondaries a zero
    wait budget
    - integrates the host interrupt waker with Arty's worker signal and
    suspension budget
    - maps explicit driver construction and cycle failures into fatal
    runtime shutdown
    - releases the final host owner during worker teardown; host `Drop`
    attempts every driver shutdown and emits diagnostics
