    fix(arty): join blocking workers during shutdown (#849)
    
    🤖 Fixes the timing-sensitive Miri live-thread failure exposed by #842.
    
    `threadpool::ThreadPool::join()` only waited for queued and active jobs.
    Its worker thread handles were detached, so Arty could finish joining
    async workers and return from `Runtime::stop()` while an `arty-blocking`
    thread was still completing thread-local destruction and exiting.
    
    This replaces the detached blocking pool with a small grow-only pool
    that retains every worker `JoinHandle`. Shutdown now closes the work
    queue, drains admitted work, and joins all blocking threads before the
    async worker exits. Worker-context shutdown still rejects self-waits,
    and saturation/growth behavior is preserved.
    
    Regression coverage installs a thread-local exit probe on a blocking
    worker and verifies that `Runtime::stop()` does not return before its
    destructor runs.
    
