    docs(thread-aware): clarify current-thread relocation (#795)
    
    ## Why
    
    Relocation may release, allocate, or initialize thread- and NUMA-local
    state. The callback therefore must execute on the thread where the value
    now runs; treating `destination` as a remote target can defeat the
    locality the API is intended to preserve.
    
    ## What changed
    
    - Clarified in the stable `ThreadAware` contract that the runtime must
    move or schedule the value first, then invoke `relocate` on the
    destination/current thread.
    - Documented that `destination` is descriptive metadata, not a request
    to run the callback elsewhere.
    - Updated the high-level crate docs, authoring guide, design notes, and
    generated READMEs with the allocator/NUMA rationale.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - `cargo test -p thread_aware_core -p thread_aware`
    - `cargo fmt -p thread_aware_core -p thread_aware -- --check`
