    full-workspace coverage. Linux x64 repeatedly reported
    `crates/seismograph_protocol/src/lib.rs:159` as uncovered even though
    `frame_size_boundaries_and_chunking_are_exact` executed that
    chunk-reading path successfully in both feature configurations.
    
    The failure was reproduced locally under the exact Linux x64 Anvil
    package selection and `target/cov` layout. With the same 7,618 passing
    tests, LLVM's LCOV export reported the line count as 0, 1, or 2 as the
    coverage build/object layout changed. The line is present in both the
    crate's `cfg(test)` unit-test build and the normal library build used by
    downstream crates; only the unit-test build originally exercised it.
    
    The suspected cause is LLVM/cargo-llvm-cov reconciliation of multiple
    coverage mappings for the same source line from those separately
    compiled crate variants. The experiments establish that the exported
    result varies despite equivalent test execution, but they do not
    establish the precise internal ordering or selection algorithm.
    
    To unblock this PR, a public-API integration test now round-trips a
    response larger than the 8 KiB frame chunk through the normal library
    build. This makes the line covered in both compilation variants, so the
    exported result remains covered regardless of how the mappings are
    reconciled. This is a targeted workaround, not a general requirement to
    duplicate unit tests as integration tests; the coverage pipeline should
    ultimately union `cfg(test)` and normal-library coverage reliably.
    
    Validation:
    - `just anvil-deny`
    - `cargo +1.96.1 clippy --package seismograph_protocol --all-targets
    --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`
    - exact Linux x64 Anvil package selection and `target/cov` layout:
      - all features: 7,619 tests passed; line 159 covered
      - no default features: 6,306 tests passed; line 159 covered
    
