    refactor(benches): adopt metabench for routerama, multitude, internity, plurality (#749)
    
    ## Summary
    
    Adopt `metabench` for the benchmark suites of `routerama`, `multitude`,
    `internity`, and `plurality`. Each crate's Criterion (wall-clock) and
    Gungraun/Callgrind (instruction-count) benchmarks are consolidated into
    a single metabench-based suite that shares benchmark identities between
    both engines, instead of maintaining separate per-engine/per-platform
    files. Each crate's `scripts/perf_report.rs` is updated to source its
    `docs/PERF.md` tables from the metabench report instead of parsing
    Criterion/Callgrind output directly, while producing the same PERF.md
    shape as before.
    
    ## Verification
    
    - `cargo check --workspace --all-features --benches`, `just clippy`,
    `just format`, `cargo test`, `cargo +nightly udeps` — all clean.
    - `just spellcheck` — clean.
    - `just readme` for all four crates — no diffs.
    - Independently reconciled every migrated benchmark's identity against
    the pre-migration originals for all four crates (accounting for
    macro-generated benchmarks) to confirm no coverage was lost. Found and
    fixed a real 2-benchmark gap in `internity`; `plurality` and `multitude`
    each gained one small additive Gungraun benchmark for a group that
    previously had no Callgrind coverage (disclosed, harmless).
    - `docs/PERF.md` regenerated for all four crates via full/default
    `perf_report.rs` runs (not `--fast`).
    - Checked `.github/workflows/main.yml` for stale references to deleted
    bench targets — none found (CI excludes crates, not individual bench
    files).
    
