    The condition types stay **private**; the wrapper exposes `is_start_failure()` / `is_bad_output()` instead, per [M-ERRORS-CANONICAL-STRUCTS](https://microsoft.github.io/rust-guidelines/guidelines/libs/ux/index.html#M-ERRORS-CANONICAL-STRUCTS). Callers therefore neither name the condition types nor import `ErrorExt`, and conditions can be added or split without breaking them.
    
