    - The `#[from]` list is written one per line as **repeated attributes**, not a multi-line list. rustfmt collapses `#[from(A, B, C)]` onto one line because it parses as a meta-list; separate `#[from(..)]` attributes accumulate (`parse_from_attribute` extends rather than replaces) and survive formatting.
