    changes how allocation reports are queried. The affected Criterion
    benchmarks also need sample-level measurement so allocation totals
    remain meaningful.
    
    ## Changes
    
    - Upgrade the workspace-managed `alloc_tracker` dependency from 0.6 to
    0.7.
    - Migrate allocation assertions to the 0.7 report API with actionable
    lookup failures.
    - Measure allocation-tracked Criterion benchmarks once per sample and
    provide the required iteration count.
    - Add shared synchronous, asynchronous, and prepared-input timing
    helpers in the internal `benchmarking` crate.
    - Keep setup and input/output teardown outside allocation measurement
    for prepared-input benchmarks.
    - Document the shared benchmark timing contract and implementation.
    
    The branch contains manual migration work and must not be recreated by
    Dependabot.
    
