    feat(multitude): add fallible streaming and generation stats (#605)
    
    ## Summary
    
    - add fallible top-level JSON array callbacks that stop immediately and
    preserve callback errors separately from JSON and limit failures
    - add `ArenaStats` generation counters for backing allocations,
    allocated bytes, cache reuse, and relocations since the last successful
    reset
    - replace the optimistic index-only refresh fixture with an
    escaped-payload global-selection workload and paired Criterion/Gungraun
    coverage
    - correct the shared Anvil Bolero recipe for cargo-bolero 0.13.4
    - bump Multitude to 0.7.1
    
    ## Selective-array decision
    
    The realistic workload did not justify a specialized public
    selected-array API. Direct `Vec<&RawValue>` indexing measured 3.66 ms /
    41.93M instructions versus 3.47 ms / 41.89M instructions for the
    existing raw callback, with higher allocation counts. This PR keeps the
    benchmark evidence but adds no selected-array API.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - `cargo test -p multitude --all-features --lib --tests --locked`
    - `cargo clippy -p multitude --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
    warnings`
    - `cargo check -p multitude --no-default-features --features
    serde_json,stats --locked`
    - short cargo-bolero 0.13.4 libfuzzer campaign using the corrected
    invocation
    - Multitude doctests, formatting, generated README check, spelling,
    Criterion, and Gungraun
    
