    ci: add cargo-machete for workspace-wide unused-dependency detection (#578)
    
    [Copilot speaking]
    
    Strengthens unused-dependency detection by adding `cargo-machete`
    alongside `cargo-udeps`, and closes a scoping gap that let unused deps
    outside a PR's diff go undetected on `main`.
    
    ## Why
    
    Two independent shortcomings:
    
    - **Detection coverage.** `cargo-udeps`, by design, ignores a needless
    direct dependency when it is still pulled in transitively, so some
    genuinely-unused deps were never flagged. `cargo-machete` uses a
    different algorithm and catches these, covering udeps' blind spot.
    - **Scoping.** The `Udeps` step lived in the `extended-analysis` job,
    which runs only on `pull_request` and was scoped to
    `exclude_not_modified` (crates whose own files changed). Any crate that
    was not modified was skipped, even when its dependency usage could have
    changed - so unused deps in such crates were never re-checked.
    
    ## Changes
    
    - Add `cargo-machete` to the toolset (`constants.env`, `setup.just`, and
    the CI setup step). It runs workspace-wide (no package selection),
    covering udeps' transitive-use blind spot and acting as the backstop for
    crates outside a PR's diff.
    - Add `just unused-dependencies-check` combining `cargo machete
    --with-metadata` + the existing `cargo udeps` pair.
    - The CI step (renamed to "Unused dependencies") now runs workspace-wide
    `cargo machete --with-metadata` and scopes `udeps` by the
    affected/impacted set (`exclude_not_affected`) rather than only modified
    crates.
    - Rename `scripts/crate-template/Cargo.toml` to `Cargo.toml.template` so
    its `{{...}}` placeholders (invalid TOML) no longer break machete's
    scan; `add-crate.ps1` restores the name when generating a crate.
    - Remove the unused dependencies flagged by machete (cachet,
    data_privacy, data_privacy_core, fetch, http_extensions, ohno). Suppress
    the sole false positive - `http_extensions`' `uuid`, used only by a
    doctest - via `[package.metadata.cargo-machete]`.
    
    ## Validation
    
    `just unused-dependencies-check` (machete + udeps) is green
    workspace-wide; the affected crates build with `--all-features
    --all-targets` and their tests and doctests pass.
    
