    perf(templated_uri): reuse the rendered path across build and routing (#559)
    
    Eliminate the redundant per-attempt template render and validation scan
    on the per-request URI construction hot path. The templated path was
    rendered twice - once in `HttpRequestBuilder::build` and again in
    `Router::resolve_request_uri` (which only swaps the base, never the
    path) - and every base join re-parsed and re-validated the whole path.
    
    - `build` now renders the path once, caches it in a `RenderedPath`
    extension, and assembles the initial `http::Uri` by reuse (new
    `Uri::to_http_uri_with_rendered`).
    - `resolve_request_uri` reuses that rendering to join only the resolved
    base on every attempt (never re-rendering), and clones the typed `Uri`
    once instead of twice.
    - `BasePath::join_path_and_query` returns the already-validated path
    directly when the base path is root (`/`), skipping the allocation and
    re-validation scan.
    
    Output-preserving (no `unsafe`), verified with differential tests.
    Benchmarks added here; the isolated `hot_path_cg` and `escaped_string`
    benches are unchanged baselines.
    
