    fix(bytesbuf): size numeric reads by T::Bytes and read unaligned for FromBytes soundness (#528)
    
    ## What
    
    Two related soundness fixes for `BytesView::get_num_{le,be,ne}` and
    their buffered fallbacks, which read a `T: FromBytes` value out of a
    byte view.
    
    ### 1. Size reads by `T::Bytes`, not `T`
    
    `FromBytes::from_*_bytes` consumes `&T::Bytes`, so every read must size,
    advance, and bound by `size_of::<T::Bytes>()` rather than
    `size_of::<T>()`. For a downstream `FromBytes` impl where the two
    differ, the old code read/advanced the wrong length and the buffered
    fallback left a `MaybeUninit<T::Bytes>` partially initialized (or
    overflowed it) before `assume_init`. For the standard integer/float
    types `Bytes = [u8; size_of::<T>()]`, so the two sizes are equal and
    this is behavior-neutral.
    
    ### 2. Read unaligned instead of building a misaligned reference
    
    The fast path constructed a `&T::Bytes` directly from an unaligned
    byte-slice pointer (`bytes.as_ptr().cast::<T::Bytes>().as_ref()`).
    `FromBytes::Bytes` is only bounded by `NumBytes` (`AsRef<[u8]>`,
    `Borrow<[u8]>`, ...), which does not guarantee an alignment of one — a
    custom impl may use a `#[repr(align(N))]` byte wrapper. For such a type
    that reference is misaligned, which is undefined behavior. The value is
    now materialized with `ptr::read_unaligned` into a properly aligned
    local. For the standard types (`Bytes = [u8; N]`, alignment 1) codegen
    is unchanged.
    
    ## Tests
    
    Added soundness coverage with custom `FromBytes` types whose `Bytes`
    associated type is wider than the value, narrower than the value, and
    over-aligned, exercising both the single-span fast path (including a
    guaranteed-misaligned source pointer) and the multi-span buffered path.
    
    ## Validation
    
    - Negative check: reverting the fix makes 6/10 of the new tests fail
    under Miri (misaligned-reference UB, uninitialized-memory UB, and
    length-assertion panics), confirming the tests are meaningful.
    - With the fix: full `bytesbuf` suite passes under Miri (186 passed, 6
    skipped) and on stable; `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D
    warnings` is clean; nightly rustfmt and spellcheck are clean.
    
