    feat(fetch): report fetch.runtime and fetch.transport telemetry attributes (#510)
    
    ## Summary
    
    Adds `fetch.runtime` and `fetch.transport` attributes identifying the
    async runtime and the transport handler used by each HTTP client. They
    are attached to the **instrumentation scope** of the client's `fetch`
    meter (both are client-scoped — a client always uses one runtime and one
    transport), so every metric the client emits inherits them without
    per-measurement overhead. This includes the hyper connection metrics,
    which are recorded against the same scoped meter handed to the transport
    via `CustomContext::meter`.
    
    These started as a single combined `fetch.transport` attribute, but that
    conflated two independent dimensions (the runtime a client is built for
    and the transport it dispatches through, which today map 1:1 but need
    not in future, e.g. an h3-on-tokio transport). Splitting them keeps each
    value a single, unambiguous word.
    
    ## Runtime and transport names
    
