    owned memory (`Block`/`SpanBuilder`), whose combined capacity is bounded
    by the virtual address space and can never exceed `usize::MAX`. Added
    comments there explaining why no check is needed, contrasting with
    `BytesView`'s shared, potentially aliased memory.
    
