    feat(templated_uri): add serde Deserialize for Uri and PathAndQuery (#473)
    
    ## Summary
    
    Adds `serde::Deserialize` (no `Serialize`) behind the existing
    default-off `serde` feature for the privacy-classified URI value types
    `Uri` and `PathAndQuery`, which previously had no serde support.
    
    Implements ADO work item AB#7422531.
    
    ## Why deserialize-only
    
    `Uri` and `PathAndQuery` are privacy-classified: they implement
    `RedactedDisplay` and return `Sensitive<String>` from `to_string()`,
    with no plain `Display`/`Serialize`. The asymmetric posture is
    intentional — classification protects values on the way **out**
    (serialize/display), while parsing untrusted input on the way **in**
    does not leak. Deserialization routes through the existing validating
    parsers (`TryFrom<String>`), reusing the owned buffer.
    
    `BaseUri`/`Origin`/`BasePath` already have symmetric serde and are
    intentionally left unchanged: they are not privacy-classified (plain
    `Display`), so serializing them is safe.
    
    ## Notes
    
