    perf(multitude): split allocator hot paths from cold refill/oversized… (#442)
    
    … tails
    
    Restructures the hot allocator paths so each public entrypoint inlines
    to a single bump-fit probe and tail-calls a `#[cold] #[inline(never)]`
    slow helper for refill and oversized-routing. The `max_normal_alloc`
    check is deferred from the hot path to the cold tail to avoid a
    two-level pointer chase through `Arc<ChunkProvider>` on every
    allocation.
    
    Affected paths:
    * `Arena::allocate_layout` / `allocate_shared_layout` (the `Allocator`
    trait impls used by `bytesbuf` and DST callers) now split into `*_slow`
    cold tails.
    * `try_alloc_slice_local_with` / `_no_drop_with` /
    `try_alloc_slice_shared_*` gain a `const PANIC: bool` parameter so
    panicking callers no longer carry a dead `Result<NonNull<_>, _>` niche
    check through the inlined fast path. Panicking siblings
    (`alloc_slice_copy`, `alloc_slice_clone_arc`, `alloc_slice_fill_*`,
    etc.) now call the helpers with `PANIC = true` directly instead of
    routing through `expect_alloc(try_*)`.
    * `alloc_uninit_box` / `_rc` / `_arc` (and the `zeroed_*` variants)
    fast-path `!needs_drop::<T>` by reusing the simpler value path, skipping
    the slice helpers per-slot init loop and noop-drop-entry reservation.
    * DST `try_reserve_dst_*` paths likewise defer the `max_normal_alloc`
    comparison into the refill branch.
    
    Other small codegen wins:
    * `CurrentChunk::bump_smart_pointers_issued` now hints `n < LARGE - 1`
    so LLVM can elide overflow guards on the `n + 1` store and subsequent
    consumers.
    * `Vec::resize` / `resize_with` route the length cursor through a
    `#[mutants::skip] inc_len` helper so `cargo-mutants` cannot mutate `+=`
    to `*=` (which would freeze the loop counter and turn length-driven
    tests into infinite-loop timeouts).
    * `align_up` is feature-gated to `cfg(feature = "dst", test)` since the
    non-DST hot paths now reconstruct the aligned pointer inline via
    `try_bump_fit`.
    
    Tests/tooling:
    * Adds `crates/multitude/scripts/correctness.rs`, a self-contained
    `cargo +nightly -Zscript` runner that reproduces CIs correctness suite
    locally: Miri (stacked borrows, tree borrows, strict provenance,
    `-Zmiri-many-seeds=0..32` race coverage), Loom, Bolero property tests,
    and `cargo-careful`.
    * Adds boundary-case tests around `MIN_MAX_NORMAL_ALLOC` and the new
    fast-path/slow-path split (kills the corresponding `>` → `>=` mutants on
    the routing decisions).
    * Adds `alloc_uninit_*` no-drop fast-path coverage and
    `allocate_layout_slow_*` mutation-killer tests.
    
    PERF.md regenerated with the post-restructure benchmark numbers.
    
