    The `FallbackPromotionPolicy` could not adequately serve the purpose of
    allowing patterns like negative caching. Usage of `get_or_insert` would
    insert into all levels of the cache regardless of the policy set on a
    fallback, since the policy was only checked on a get hit. This change
    moves policy checks to the `CacheWrapper` implementation of `insert`, so
    that it is always applied to each tier individually. It also renames it
    to `InsertPolicy` for clarity.

