    fix(ohno_macros): remove redundant `}}` arm in parse_display_template (#395)
    
    The dedicated `'}' if chars.peek() == Some(&'}')` arm was functionally
    equivalent to the `_ => result.push(ch)` fallback: both produce the same
    `}}` sequence in the resulting format string, which `format!` interprets
    as a literal `}`. Because the two paths are observationally identical,
    no test could distinguish them — the mutation `if chars.peek() ==
    Some(&'}')` -> `if false` survived, and the function had to be excluded
    from mutation testing via `#[cfg_attr(test, mutants::skip)]`.
    
    Removing the redundant arm eliminates the untestable branch and allows
    mutation testing to apply to the rest of the function. All 137 existing
    `ohno_macros` tests continue to pass; the
    `test_parse_display_template_escaped_braces` cases (`{{static}}`,
    `{field}}`, `{{Error}}: {field} {{end}}`) all still produce the exact
    same generated tokens, confirming behavioral equivalence.
    
