    feat(http_extensions): add request/response timeouts and refactor body builder (#362)
    
    Adds response-level and body-level idle timeouts to `http_extensions`,
    introduces `HttpBodyOptions` for per-body configuration, and
    restructures the body module.
    
    ### Timeouts
    
    - `TimeoutBody` wraps streaming bodies with an idle timer that resets on
    each frame. On timeout, returns an error and drops the inner body;
    subsequent polls return `None` consistent with `is_end_stream()`.
    - `ResponseTimeout` / `BodyTimeout` extension types attach to requests
    for middleware to enforce.
    - `HttpRequestBuilder` gains `response_timeout()`, `body_timeout()`, and
    `timeout()` convenience methods.
    
    ### Body options
    
    - New `HttpBodyOptions` with `timeout` and `buffer_limit` fields;
    per-call options merge on top of builder-level defaults.
    - `body()` and `stream()` now accept `&HttpBodyOptions`; replaces the
    old `external()` method.
    
    ### Refactor
    
    - Splits `body.rs` into `body/{mod, builder, options, timeout_body}.rs`.
    - Renames `creator`/`create_body` to `builder` throughout.
    - Fixes doc examples to be self-contained and runnable.
    
    ### Testing
    
    All new types and methods are covered: `TimeoutBody`
    happy/timeout/post-timeout paths, `BodyTimeout`/`ResponseTimeout`,
    `HttpBodyOptions` merge semantics, and the new builder methods.
    
