    feat(bytesbuf): add bytesbuf_global_pool_instances_total metric (#352)
    
    Track how many GlobalPoolInner instances are created so application
    owners can detect excessive pool creation instead of reuse.
    
    Each GlobalPoolInner owns its own memory capacity, and in typical usage
    a thread-aware GlobalPool creates at most one per thread. A high count
    from this metric indicates something is creating pools instead of
    reusing existing ones.
    
