    feat(bytesbuf): make BytesBufWriter owning via into_writer() (#274)
    
    ## Summary
    
    `BytesBuf` now exposes an owning writer cycle:
    
    `BytesBuf::into_writer(memory) -> BytesBufWriter<M> ->
    BytesBufWriter::into_inner() -> BytesBuf`
    
    This replaces the previous referencing writer adapter and keeps write
    behavior unchanged.
    
    ## Changes
    
    - Renamed the write adapter type from `BytesBufWrite` to
    `BytesBufWriter` and kept it publicly re-exported from the crate root.
    - Changed `BytesBuf::as_write()`/`writer()` style borrowing API to an
    owning `BytesBuf::into_writer(memory)` API.
    - Refactored `BytesBufWriter` to own both `BytesBuf` and memory provider
    `M` by value, and added `into_inner()` to recover the buffer.
    - Added `impl<M: Memory + ?Sized> Memory for &M` so reference memory
    handles (including `&dyn Memory`) work with `into_writer`.
    - Renamed internal module file `write_adapter.rs` to `buf_writer.rs` to
    match the type role.
    - Included the existing repository-level `AGENTS.md` guidance update in
    this PR diff (no manual changelog edits).
    
